### Step 1: Bug Scenario Image Analysis

The image shows a VoiceOver tooltip reading:  
"Option 4 Option 4, selected (5 of 6)"

This indicates that the screen reader is reading the dropdown item label twice, which matches the bug report: "Voiceover reads dropdown items twice".

### Step 2: Bug Root Cause Reasoning

From the bug report and the code, the likely cause is that both the `title` attribute and the visible text content are being set on the dropdown menu item. Screen readers will often read both the `title` and the text content, resulting in the label being read twice.

In the code, this is the relevant part:
```jsx
<ListBox.MenuItem
  key={itemProps.id}
  isActive={selectedItem === item}
  isHighlighted={
    highlightedIndex === index || selectedItem === item
  }
  title={itemToElement ? item.text : itemToString(item)}
  {...itemProps}>
  {itemToElement ? (
    <ItemToElement key={itemProps.id} {...item} />
  ) : (
    itemToString(item)
  )}
  {selectedItem === item && (
    <Checkmark16
      className={`${prefix}--list-box__menu-item__selected-icon`}
    />
  )}
</ListBox.MenuItem>
```
The `title` prop is being set to the same value as the visible text, which causes VoiceOver to read both.

### Step 3: Bug Location

The bug is in the `title` prop of `<ListBox.MenuItem ... title={...} ...>`.  
**To fix:** Only set the `title` attribute if the item is being rendered as a custom element (`itemToElement`), not when it's just a string (since the text is already visible).

